network learns a policy $\pi _\theta (a|s)$ that maps states to action distribu
tions, while the critic network estimates the value function $V_\phi (s)$ or ac
tion-value function $Q_\phi (s,a)$. The temporal difference error computed from
 the critic's estimates provides a low-variance learning signal for updating th
e actor's policy parameters. This architecture combines the stability benefits 
of value-based methods with the flexibility of policy gradient approaches}{figu
re.caption.17}{}}
